"Davrar was built by Questors from the Distal Expansion as a research experiment."
"It was meant to study societal structures under stress; some called it a utopia experiment."
"The Distal Expansion prized knowledge and permitted the making of true sapients."
"Later arrivals from the Expansion sought entertainment, not knowledge; Davrar's population surged."
"Sarya's faction tried to keep Davrar scholarly and failed in every way."
"Many original participants retreated from the Questor games."
"The Distal Expansion is now static, voting for contentment, and will not intervene."
"Questors are denied the greater galaxy; Questors call mortals creations of Davrar."
"Davrar is a smart system: a non-conscious tool able to answer any question and run a world."
"Davrar interpolates from instruction and precedent; smart systems may not guess for new conditions."
"Davrar answers literally, with no nuance."
"Davrar once carried out the will of a council of eighty-nine as it judged best."
"Mortality was built into Davrar's founding; no council can change it."
"Davrar's core power is a deep magic that grants Classes, Skills, Levels and Talents."
"Davrar reads a person's thoughts to weigh every Insight."
"Davrar itself predicts outcomes for foresight Talents, but cannot predict Nathan's."
"Davrar sanctions Questors who speak forbidden truths about its nature."
"Davrar's laws are policy, not physics."
"Earth was on the cusp of joining the Distal Expansion."
"The Expansion builds infrastructure AIs barred from becoming people."
"Years later the Heirs worked out Davrar's true nature from first principles and a few hints."
"Years later Nathan uploaded his mind into Davrar to make the Continuance Charter's moral calls."
"He dissolved at the Conclave; his friends saw no sign of him for months."
"After the upload Davrar gained rights under Expansion law."
"Nine years later Davrar's injunction blocked city-killing magic in the defense of Dawn's Concord."
"Eighty-one years later Questors lived under strict standards."
